# Gave permission by assigning user in Authentik groups

• Dont give permission directly to a user, instead create Authentik group & add user to this group

## Example: User asked to create "Медиа - команду", Team Folder & Docs in Nextcloud:

1. Add groups to the right YAML under [permissions](instance/maps/permissions/Readme.md)
2. apply Authentik
3. apply Nextcloud
4. login user (using n8n workflow)

# When integrate new app with Authentik, behind reverse-proxy 

Goal: manage users access
0. Read application's docs — both `{app}/README.md` + `{app}/docs/` and `instance/{app}/Readme.md`:
1. If theres multiple integrations options (eg IdP, OIDC...) - Ask user
Tell user results of each options: preffered: IdP (so all user managment in single place - Authentik)